MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Crossfade feels like a natural next choice because its melodic hard rock connects with what draws me to One Day Remains and Seventeen Days: strong melodies with enough weight behind them.",
    "Hypnotize, Once More 'Round the Sun, and Fury of Our Maker's Hand appeal through different parts of my heavier listening: aggressive vocals, adventurous rhythms, and forceful grooves. Those connections fit my interest in 10.000 Days and Soundtrack to Your Escape."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Stadium Arcadium is related to my broader rock listening, but its funk rock direction does not satisfy my current appetite for heavier riffs and intensity.",
    "Scream is too ambiguous for me to connect confidently with my interests. Mutter and Worship Music do fit, but I would postpone them because the other albums appeal more strongly today."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interest in rock seems to have been stretched too broadly when it led to Stadium Arcadium; being connected to rock is less important to me right now than the particular weight and energy.",
    "Heavy riffs alone do not make every album equally compelling. Several heavier recommendations fit my taste without giving me as strong a reason to choose them as Hypnotize or Crossfade."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My latest listening to Ten Thousand Fists and 10.000 Days makes the combination of heaviness, memorable melodies, and rhythmic variety especially relevant to what I want next.",
    "I choose selectively even among albums that suit me. A clear connection to a particular part of my listening matters more than a general resemblance, and an ambiguous title leaves me without that connection."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations mostly understood my interest in heavy, melodic rock, but sometimes treated broad rock connections or heaviness alone as enough to make an album a priority."
}
